l","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{G}{G}","name":"Sylvan Basilisk","oracle_id":"4f348e7a-fe13-4621-bd88-5d2fb5b597f2","oracle_text":"Whenever this creature becomes blocked by a creature, destroy that creature.","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2007-07-13","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Basilisk"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":["B"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{B}","name":"Walking Corpse","oracle_id":"fea95888-e16a-4209-9cd4-623f7f4d2f67","oracle_text":"","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-07-03","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Zombie"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Defender"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{U}","name":"Wall of Tears","oracle_id":"5825d718-6a32-4f4c-9b56-1a50051cfe28","oracle_text":"Defender (This creature can't attack.)\nWhenever this creature blocks a creature, return that creature to its owner's hand at end of combat.","power":"0","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"1998-03-02","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Wall"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"The color of the blocking/blocked creature is checked only at declaration of the block. If the creature is green or white at that time, it will be destroyed at end of combat even if it changes color before combat ends.","oracle_id":"2c57c4e9-0a46-45d6-92db-9203fb722b60","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Affected creatures lose all other colors and are mono-black.","oracle_id":"5667376e-e59c-4b17-b096-5d92cdfe3db1","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Arrogant Bloodlord becomes blocked by multiple creatures with power 1 or less, its ability triggers that many times. Each of those abilities will cause it to be destroyed separately (in case Arrogant Bloodlord isn't destroyed the first time due to an Aura with umbra armor, for example). The same is true if it somehow blocks multiple creatures with power 1 or less.","oracle_id":"a35e1882-b878-49cf-a06c-be12a06d4977","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Arrogant Bloodlord blocks or becomes blocked by a creature whose power is 2 or greater, Arrogant Bloodlord's ability won't trigger. It still won't trigger if the other creature's power changes to 1 or less later in combat.","oracle_id":"a35e1882-b878-49cf-a06c-be12a06d4977","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The power of the other creature is checked only when it blocks or becomes blocked by Arrogant Bloodlord. Once the Bloodlord's ability triggers, it will be destroyed at end of combat (after combat damage has been dealt) even if the other creature's power changes before then.","oracle_id":"a35e1882-b878-49cf-a06c-be12a06d4977","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability destroys the creature at the end of the combat, which is after all first strike and normal damage dealing is done. This means that a creature may have to regenerate twice to survive the combat, once from damage and once again at end of combat.","oracle_id":"af354337-424c-4c7e-8ca5-6149261368d2","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gorgon Recluse's ability triggers when it blocks or becomes blocked by a nonblack creature and creates a delayed triggered ability that will destroy that creature at the end of combat step. It destroys that creature then even if Gorgon Recluse doesn't survive that long or the creature somehow becomes black.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A card with madness that's discarded counts as having been discarded even though it's put into exile rather than a graveyard. If it was discarded to pay a cost, that cost is still paid. Abilities that trigger when a card is discarded will still trigger.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A spell cast for its madness cost is put onto the stack like any other spell. It can be countered, copied, and so on. As it resolves, it's put onto the battlefield if it's a permanent card or into its owner's graveyard if it's an instant or sorcery card.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cards are discarded in a Magic game only from a player's hand. Effects that put cards into a player's graveyard from anywhere else do not cause those cards to be discarded.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Casting a spell with madness ignores the timing rules based on the card's card type. For example, you can cast a sorcery with madness if you discard it during an opponent's turn.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you choose not to cast a card with madness when the madness triggered ability resolves, it's put into your graveyard. Madness doesn't give you another chance to cast it later.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you discard a card with madness to pay the cost of a spell or activated ability, that card's madness triggered ability (and the spell that card becomes, if you choose to cast it) will resolve before the spell or ability the discard paid for.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you discard a card with madness while a spell or ability is resolving, it moves immediately to exile. Continue resolving that spell or ability, noting that the card you discarded is not in your graveyard at this time. Its madness triggered ability will be placed onto the stack once that spell or ability has completely resolved.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Madness works independently of why you're discarding the card. You could discard it to pay a cost, because a spell or ability tells you to, or because you have too many cards in your hand during your cleanup step. You can't discard a card with madness just because you want to, though.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a madness cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined by only its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast that spell was.","oracle_id":"e6c9a699-0468-42f8-aad5-b9d45a3c1d37","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
